<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111743" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλέγρα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλεγμόν-ρη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Phlegra,</i>
			an ancient name for Pallene in Thrace, prob. from its
			<i>volcanic</i> nature, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				7
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φλέγρας πεδίον,</span> in which
			the giants are said to have been conquered by the gods, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				1.67
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				824
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φλεγραία πλάξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					295
				</span></i>
			: pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φλέγραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					6(5).33
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
